  "scope": "Per-input/document batch unbinned histogram statistics review and opt-in CSV through C++/Python and both shared ImGui launchers.",
  "semantics": "Retain scalar statistics from existing ordered-stage histogram results, never reconstructed from bin centers. Finite ROI range outliers contribute to extrema/mean/population SD/sum. Detached rows contain identity/options/type/policy/counts but no snapshots/provider/bin arrays; Python returns owning copies. Default file products and existing live/saved session Results tables are preserved. encoded_bytes remains actual encoded output bytes.",
  "transport": "Opt-in one <output_stem>.histograms.csv per input with histogram rows, after bins/exports and before complete session. New-files-only preflight/consent/cancel/partial/no-retry rules remain. CSV indices are zero-based, counters exact UInt64, values max_digits10/classic locale, absent statistics blank. Immutable setup export intent writes closed V2 only when enabled; V1 unchanged and V2 false canonicalizes to V1. Consent is not serialized.",
  "ui": "Both shared ImGui launchers review a clipped summary table and export checkbox. Choice changes invalidate preparation/confirmation/consent. Saved setup restores the flag without consent. Summaries remain inspectable after Apply or partial publication.",
  "memory": "Cumulative detached summary storage and optional CSV formatting scratch are conservatively admitted before kernels/publication; formatter validates scalar rows and checkpoints during batch work. Frontend copies, provider caches, allocator overhead and process RSS remain external.",
  "verification": "589 selected Python checks per OS including 24 new API and ten new input checks; five native executable suites per OS and fresh installed SDK consumers. Independent readers verify 84 reports / 23800 raw input frames, including 20 new reports / 2056 frames. Tests cover unbinned ROI/range-outlier/NaN/empty populations, exact UInt64 counters and CSV quoting, immutable detached copies, output counts/memory limits, cancellation/conflicts/partial publication and closed V2 setup save/load. No complete ImageJ/Fiji source/reference/resource/real-GPU/OS-desktop/platform acceptance.",
